# Chat round 5 — full-area picker and message scrolling

Generated with built-in image_gen. The user accepted the direction with “great” before moving to annotation needs analysis. Both images are planning references subject to the reservations below, not pixel-perfect specifications or MVP acceptance. Original review indices were generated image 0 and generated image 1, excluding the previously inspected reference.

## Image 0 — expanded chat picker

![Expanded chat picker](01-full-chat-picker.png)

The picker covers the complete chat content area below its toolbar, including transcript, run strip and composer. The selected-conversation dropdown remains available and toggles the panel closed. Five top-level sections have their own scroll areas and four horizontal splitters: New, Later, Active, Channels, History.

| Section | Membership |
| --- | --- |
| New | Channel notifications qualify on explicit mention, when the user is the only human, or on configured notification for changes. Example chips illustrate the qualifying reason; the chips themselves remain a design proposal. |
| Later | Explicit user movement from New; reading does not fill or clear it automatically. |
| Active | Any chat with at least one running agent instance, including channels. Queued-only chats do not qualify. |
| Channels | All channels, including those simultaneously in New, Later or Active. |
| History | Recency bush of every non-channel chat, including any also shown in Active or attention groups. |

Repeated entries share the same conversation identity. General appears in New, Active and Channels; Investigate preview failure appears in Active and History. Changes and selection operate on that shared identity, not separate copied records. New qualification for non-channel chats was not newly specified by this clarification; do not silently infer a different rule from the channel examples.

## Image 1 — internal message scrollbars and one timing row

![Message scrolling and timing](02-message-scroll-and-timing.png)

Human and final-agent message bodies scroll independently after a configurable maximum height. Author headers, timing and execution-history controls remain outside those message-body scroll areas. The outer transcript has its own scrollbar. No message-collapse or Show less controls remain.

One compact row places 1m 30s outside the rectangle on the left. Its segments combine model time with tool totals grouped by tool identity: Model 30s, Read 12s, Search 18s, Test 30s. This example is serial; actual concurrent durations must not be misleadingly summed as elapsed wall time. Tool-detail overlay remains for implementation review.

The accepted earlier-turn/tool-call history entry, direct running-instance navigation/Stop and shared empty composer are preserved. A completed response does not remove another running instance of the same agent.

## Reservations

- Splitter adjustment, scroll independence, dropdown toggling, membership and restored reading position are implementation requirements; static images demonstrate layout only.
- Initial section heights are illustrative and adjustable. No user preference for exact equal dimensions was established.
- Single chevrons remain at some scrollbar ends despite the shared double-chevron requirement. Avatars and view controls still need tighter sizing. BA avatar in the run strip must match its message identity; generation retained an inconsistent identicon.
- Timing segment proportions are approximate in the image. Implement measured proportions, tool aggregation independent of arguments, and truthful handling of concurrency/unknown time.
- Board is unchanged context and does not supersede the accepted board design or existing reservations.
- All messages, timings, counts and results are illustrative. No runtime implementation, test execution or agent activity was performed by generating these mockups.

